# Main plot range preview

## Pre-work plan

- Background: user requested a live translucent range preview for non-CURSOR main TA plot drag through Daedilus message `msg-fsi-1bd89346d2a14bbfba8fdbe0682c8219`.
- Goal: add one browser-local preview overlay and stable DOM diagnostics without changing existing range commit semantics.
- Scope/owner: Dynamic Renderer source/direct tests, exact package versions, current RFC/WBS/Test/DevLog; Daedilus owns consumer Playwright source and real-browser evidence.
- Invariants: CURSOR pan unchanged; non-CURSOR pointerup commit unchanged; preview is pointer-inert, normalized, nonzero only after movement, and cleared on up/cancel/lifecycle end; external dirty paths untouched.
- Steps: RFC -> inspect exact main plot render/gesture seam -> RED focused tests -> minimal implementation -> owner tests/build/package -> package handoff -> consumer real rerun.
- Acceptance: left/right preview visible during drag with positive width; stable testid/attributes; cleared after up/cancel; existing direct suites green and immutable package evidence supplied.
- Risk: reactive SVG replacement could orphan preview state or intercept pointer events; use the existing plot SVG and document-level gesture lifetime.
- Stop condition: no wire/action change; if implementation would require changing non-CURSOR commit semantics, stop and return to design.

